<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Bank of Ireland lists ADRs on NYSE.</title>
<headline>Bank of Ireland lists ADRs on NYSE.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of Ireland said on Wednesday its stock had begun trading on the New York Stock Exchange (NYSE) on September 17 in the form of American depositary receipts (ADRs).</p>
<p>The bank said in a statement that each American depositary share represented four units of Bank of Ireland ordinary stock and would be evidenced by one ADR.</p>
<p>Bank of Ireland added that the Bank of New York would act as depositary for the ADRs.</p>
<p>--Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
